# XSH tss_get(), tss_set()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Setting a value from a destructor beyond the second call (lost storage or
# endless repetition) is unspecified and not exercised.

assertion  XSH.tss_get.001
anchor     functions/tss_get.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/tss_get.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       tss_set() returns thrd_success and tss_get() then returns the
           pointer stored, including after it is replaced by another and by a
           null pointer.
test       t/001-set-get.c

assertion  XSH.tss_get.002
anchor     functions/tss_get.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/tss_get.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       A value set in one thread is not seen in another: a new thread
           sees null, sets its own, and the creator's value is unchanged
           while the new thread still holds its own.
test       t/002-per-thread.c

assertion  XSH.tss_get.003
anchor     functions/tss_get.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       Replacing a non-null value with tss_set() calls no destructor; at
           the thread's end the destructor is called once, with the last
           value.
test       t/003-set-no-destructor.c

assertion  XSH.tss_get.004
anchor     functions/tss_get.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       While a key's destructor runs at thread exit, tss_get() for that
           key returns a null pointer.
test       t/004-null-in-destructor.c

assertion  XSH.tss_get.005
anchor     functions/tss_get.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       A destructor that calls tss_set() for its own key (once) sees
           tss_get() return the new value.
test       t/005-set-in-destructor.c
